        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nDesign a skill assessment\u00a0questioner for R (Programming Language).\n\n###Response to evaluate:\n1. What is the main purpose of using functions in R?\nA. To create reusable code\nB. To store and retrieve data\nC. To create graphics\nD. To process calculations \n\n2. What is the difference between 'data.frame' and 'matrix' in R?\nA. Data.frame is used to store and manipulate numerical values, whereas matrix is used to store and manipulate character values\nB. Data.frame is used to store and manipulate character values, whereas matrix is used to store and manipulate numerical values\nC. Data.frame is used to create graphs, whereas matrix is used to perform calculations\nD. Data.frame is used to process calculations, whereas matrix is used to create graphs \n\n3. What is the 'ifelse' function used for in R?\nA. To compare two data sets and return a value accordingly\nB. To create conditional statements\nC. To assign values to a given condition\nD. To calculate mean, median and mode of a data set\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response offer direct, pertinent, and valuable information that actively assists the user's query or concern in a dialogue? The response should align with the user's needs and offer proactive suggestions or advice, if applicable.]\nScore 1: The model's