        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nCompare and contrast Java and JavaScript\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nJava and JavaScript are two of the most popular programming languages today, but they have significant differences. Java is an object-oriented language, meaning it is designed to create and manipulate objects; Java code is compiled, meaning it must first be written and tested before it can be run; and it is platform-independent, meaning it can run on any platform without any changes. JavaScript, on the other hand, is a scripting language; it is interpreted, not compiled, so it does not require the same level of testing; and it is platform-dependent, meaning it must be adapted to the platform it is running on. Another important difference is that Java code is threads- safe, meaning it can safely operate on multiple tasks at the same time, while JavaScript code is not threads-safe and should therefore only be run on a single thread.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response offer direct, pertinent, and valuable information that actively assists the user's query or concern in a dialogue? The response should align with the user's needs and offer proactive suggestions or advice, if applicable.]\nScore 1: The model's response is completely off-topic and offers no helpful information or direction in relation to t