        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nGenerate a children's story with the following title: The Magic Violin.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nOnce upon a time, there was a young girl named Sofia who had a magical violin. Sofia had always dreamed of playing music but had never received any lessons. One day, while walking through the woods near her home, Sofia stumbled upon an old violin case, and when her curiosity got the better of her, she opened it. To her surprise, the violin started singing to her, and a bright light filled the air. Sofia knew she had been given a very special gift.\n\nSofia couldn't wait to try out her new violin, so she ran home and started playing. To her surprise, music started pouring out of the instrument, like a river of joy. She played and played, and soon her magical violin brought her good luck and happiness in every situation.\n\nSofia started entering violin competitions and won every time. The judges were amazed by her playing and asked how she did it. Sofia simply replied that her magical violin helped her. She even formed an orchestra with other musicians from the village, and the magic of her violin inspired them all to play beautiful music.\n\nThe Magic Violin brings joy to people all around the world and spreads happiness wherever it goes.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's respon