        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nWrite a short story around the setting of a jungle.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nJohn had always wanted to explore the jungle. He dreamed of darting through the lush green foliage, discovering hidden waterfalls and ancient ruins, and most of all meeting the mysterious, exotic creatures that lived in the jungle. \n\nSo one day he made the brave decision to take the first step and to set out on his journey. He had no idea what to expect, but he was determined to find out. \n\nThe jungle was unlike anything he had ever seen before. Vibrant colors and strange, ghostly sounds greeted him as he stepped outside, and the air was filled with an energizing warmth. He quickly learned to navigate the twists and turns of the jungle, and soon found himself in a clearing with a majestic waterfall. \n\nHe stood mesmerized as the vivid blue water gently fell from the cliffs, feeling both awed and inspired by the beauty of God's creation. He also spotted a few colorful birds and small mammals along the way which added to his exploration. \n\nAs the sun set and the sky turned a beautiful orange and pink, John felt a sense of peace and joy he had never experienced before. He had truly found a new home in the jungle, and he was determined to keep exploring and discovering its secrets. \n\n\n###Score Rubr