        "rejected_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nWrite a short story around the setting of a jungle.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nThe Jungle\n\nMartin stepped into the jungle, feeling awe-filled and excited. The air was damp and heavy, and the trees loomed overhead, their canopies creating a ceiling of lush, vibrant green. He could smell the damp earth and the sweet scent of wildflowers. Martin took a deep breath and smiled. \n\nHe walked deeper and deeper into the jungle, untouched and untrampled, and his excitement grew. He soon came upon a clearing and saw a beautiful waterfall in the center. He was mesmerized by the sight of it and the sun sparkling off the many droplets of water. \n\nHe ventured closer and when he was close enough, he could hear the sound of the water, like a lullaby. Martin felt a sense of peace wash over him and he laughed, feeling so happy to be in the jungle. He wanted to explore and see what else he could find. \n\nHe turned and continued walking, and soon his explorations led him to a large cave. He peered in and was amazed with what he saw. Inside was a room full of crystals, dazzling and colorful, like a bouquet of gems. Martin was astounded and looked up at the night sky, marveling at the beauty of the jungle. \n\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response offer direct, pertinent, and valuable 