        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nWrite a summary about the D-DAY Invasion.\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nD-Day, also known as Operation Overlord, was the codename for the Allied operation that launched the successful invasion of German-occupied France during World War II. On June 6th, 1944, over 156,000 Allied troops landed along a 50-mile stretch of the French coastline between the Cotentin Peninsula and the town of Cherbourg. This massive military operation marked the beginning of the end of the war in Europe and was a major turning point in the conflict. \n\nThe D-Day invasion was an unprecedented logistical feat. Allied forces created an elaborate network of sea and airborne transportation to move men and supplies from England to the beaches of Normandy. They also used deception operations to fool the Germans into thinking the invasion would take place further south than it actually did. In the end, the D-Day invasion worked as planned, and the Allies were able to establish a beachhead in Europe that enabled them to bring the war to a close in Europe only a few months later.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response offer direct, pertinent, and valuable information that actively assists the user's query or concern in a dialogue? The response should align with the user's needs and offer proactive suggestion