        "chosen_instruction": "###Task Description:\nAn instruction (might include an Input inside it), a response to evaluate, and a score rubric representing a evaluation criteria are given.\n1. Write a detailed feedback that assess the quality of the response strictly based on the given score rubric, not evaluating in general.\n2. After writing a feedback, write a score that is an integer between 1 and 5. You should refer to the score rubric.\n3. The output format should look as follows: \"Feedback: (write a feedback for criteria) [RESULT] (an integer number between 1 and 5)\"\n4. Please do not generate any other opening, closing, and explanations.\n\n###The instruction to evaluate:\nGenerate a piece of children's literature that highlights the importance of friendship\n\n###Response to evaluate:\nOnce upon a time, there were two best friends: Fiz and Fab. Fiz was a penguin, and Fab was an anteater. They loved exploring their world together, and having fun.\n\nOne day, they stumbled across an new and exciting ice cream parlor. It was wonderful! The two of them shared all sorts of delicious flavors, and chatted until the sun rose. They made plans to come back again the next day, and the next.\n\nWhen summer came, they visited the ice cream parlor daily- sometimes even twice a day! Their friendship had only grown stronger, and the ice cream parlor was their favorite place to hang out.\n\nEventually, Fab shared a secret with Fiz- he was sad because he couldn't find any other anteaters to be friends with. Fiz was determined to fix the problem, and she embarked on a journey around the world to find Fab's friends.\n\nFinally, after days and days of travel, Fiz found Fab's missing friends, and they all had the best ice cream party ever. Everyone had lots of fun, and friendship was endlessly praised.  From then on, they never forgot the importance of friendship, and always cherished their bond.\n\n###Score Rubrics:\n[Does the model's response offer direct, pertinent, and